# The closed Backend Variant vocabulary (Story 5.1, FR-3, AD-15; decisions/ESC-5.1-1.md).
#
# Every Expectations line's `variant` and every Inventory `backends` value must
# be listed here; `bun run expectations:init` and `bun run expectations:check`
# fail on anything else. A Test ID's Variants are exactly its Inventory
# `backends`. Besides the alpha Variants and the AC's examples, this lists the
# post-alpha backends the Inventory already tags (`mariadb`, `mysql`, `sqlsrv`,
# `queue-beanstalkd@beanstalkd`), per ESC-5.1-1, so the denominator stays full.
# Which Variants are alpha is defined by PRD SM-1 and AD-28, not here.
#
# Format: UTF-8, LF, one Variant per line, sorted by UTF-16 code units and
# unique. Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored. A Variant is
# `<backend>` (`^[a-z0-9]+$`) or `<driver>@<backend>`
# (`^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*@[a-z0-9]+$`).

mariadb
mysql
none
pgsql
queue-beanstalkd@beanstalkd
queue-database@pgsql
queue-database@sqlite
queue-redis@redis
queue-sync@none
redis
session-redis@redis
sqlite
sqlsrv
